## QUIT
QUIT FORCE/S

Quit DeluxeMusic.
- FORCE -- Quit without asking to save unsaved changes

## NEW
NEW

Open a new blank score document.

## OPEN
OPEN FILENAME,FORCE/S

Open an existing score file.
- FILENAME -- Path to the score file (CMUS, DMCS, or MIDI format)
- FORCE -- Discard unsaved changes without asking

Example: OPEN "Work:Scores/MySong.CMUS"

## CLOSE
CLOSE FORCE/S

Close the current score.
- FORCE -- Close without asking to save

## SAVE
SAVE

Save the current score to its existing filename.

## SAVEAS
SAVEAS FILENAME,FORMAT/K,EMBEDSAMPLES/K,FORCE/S

Save the current score with options. If FILENAME is omitted, the file requester appears.
- FILENAME -- Destination path
- FORMAT -- File format: CMUS, SMF (Standard MIDI File), SMUS (IFF Simple Music),
  REQUEST (opens the format selection requester).
  If omitted, uses the format from the previous save.
- EMBEDSAMPLES -- ON, OFF, or TOGGLE. Controls the "Embed Samples" switch.
- FORCE -- Overwrite without asking

Example: SAVEAS "Work:Scores/Song.CMUS" FORMAT CMUS EMBEDSAMPLES ON
Example: SAVEAS "Work:Scores/Song.mid" FORMAT SMF

## REVERT
REVERT FORCE/S

Revert to previously saved version of the score.
- FORCE -- Revert without confirmation

## PRINT
PRINT OPTIONS/S

Print the score.
- OPTIONS -- Open the Print As... dialog instead of printing directly

## UNDO
UNDO

Undo the last operation.

## COPY
COPY

Copy selected items to the clipboard.

## CUT
CUT

Cut selected items to the clipboard.

## PASTE
PASTE

Paste from clipboard into the score at the cursor position.

## PLAY
PLAY SECTION/S

Play the score.
- SECTION -- Play only the currently selected section (between section bars)

## STOP
STOP

Stop playback.

## RESUME
RESUME

Resume playback from where it was last stopped.

## CHANGEWINDOW
CHANGEWINDOW LEFT/N,TOP/N,WIDTH/N,HEIGHT/N

Move and resize the current window.
- LEFT -- X position in pixels
- TOP -- Y position in pixels
- WIDTH -- Width in pixels
- HEIGHT -- Height in pixels

## SIZEWINDOW
SIZEWINDOW WIDTH/N,HEIGHT/N

Resize the main document window.
- WIDTH -- New width in pixels
- HEIGHT -- New height in pixels

## WINDOW
WINDOW NAMES/M,OPEN/S,CLOSE/S,SNAPSHOT/S,ACTIVATE/S,MIN/S,MAX/S,FRONT/S,BACK/S,PREV/S,NEXT/S

Open, close, activate, or resize named windows.
- NAMES -- One or more window names:
  DOCUMENT       Main document window
  TIMESIG        "Set Time Signature" window
  KEYSIG         "Set Key Signature" window
  CLEF           "Set Clef" window
  TEMPO          "Set Tempo" window
  INSTRUMENT     "Set Instrument" window
  PRINT          Print Options window
  SCOREPREFS     Score Settings window
  STAVEPREFS     Stave Settings window
  DISPLAYPREFS   Display Preferences window
  MIDI_WINDOW    MIDI Settings window
  REVEAL         Reveal Project window
  INFO           About box
  FKEY           "Assign macro to key" window
  HELP           Help window
  TOOLBAR        Toolbar window
  KEYBOARD       Keyboard window
- OPEN -- Open the window, or bring to front if already open
- CLOSE -- Close the window
- SNAPSHOT -- Save current position/size
- ACTIVATE -- Activate the window
- MIN/MAX -- Minimize or maximize (document windows only)
- FRONT/BACK -- Move in front of or behind other windows
- PREV/NEXT -- Activate previous/next document (document windows only)

Example: WINDOW TOOLBAR OPEN
Example: WINDOW INSTRUMENT CLOSE
Example: WINDOW DOCUMENT MAX FRONT

## MOVEWINDOW
MOVEWINDOW LEFT/N,TOP/N

Move a window to a new position.
- LEFT -- X position in pixels
- TOP -- Y position in pixels

## SCREENTOFRONT
SCREENTOFRONT

Move the DeluxeMusic screen to the front.

## SCREENTOBACK
SCREENTOBACK

Move the DeluxeMusic screen to the back.

## LOCKDISPLAY
LOCKDISPLAY

Inhibit screen refreshes. Use during batch ARexx operations for speed.
Always pair with UNLOCKDISPLAY.

## UNLOCKDISPLAY
UNLOCKDISPLAY

Re-enable screen refreshes after LOCKDISPLAY.

## UPDATEDISPLAY
UPDATEDISPLAY FORCE/S

Refresh the display.
- FORCE -- Force complete redraw

## LOCKGUI
LOCKGUI

Inhibit all keyboard and mouse input. Use during batch ARexx operations.
Always pair with UNLOCKGUI.

## UNLOCKGUI
UNLOCKGUI

Re-enable keyboard and mouse input after LOCKGUI.

## BEEPSCREEN
BEEPSCREEN

Beep or flash the screen.

## SETSTATUSBAR
SETSTATUSBAR TITLE

Place a message in the program's title bar.
- TITLE -- Text to display

Example: SETSTATUSBAR "Processing..."

## SAVESETTINGS
SAVESETTINGS

Save the GUI settings (window positions, macro assignments, etc.) to tooltypes.

## SETTOOL
SETTOOL TOOL/A

Select a tool in the tool window.
- TOOL -- Tool name: MOVEMENT, DELETE, NOTE, GROUP, DYNAMIC, TEXT

Example: SETTOOL NOTE

## SETACCIDENTAL
SETACCIDENTAL VALUE/A,UPDATE/S

Change the accidental setting in the tool window.
- VALUE -- NATURAL, SHARP, FLAT, DOUBLESHARP, DOUBLEFLAT, NONE
- UPDATE -- Also update any currently selected notes

## SETDIVISION
SETDIVISION VALUE/A,UPDATE/S

Change the note duration setting in the tool window.
- VALUE -- D (double whole), 1 (whole), 2 (half), 4 (quarter), 8 (eighth), 16, 32, 64
  Append "R" for rest, e.g. "16R" = 16th-note rest
- UPDATE -- Also update any currently selected notes

Example: SETDIVISION 4
Example: SETDIVISION 16R

## SETDOT
SETDOT VALUE/A,UPDATE/S

Change the dotted note setting.
- VALUE -- NONE, DOT, DOUBLEDOT
- UPDATE -- Also update any currently selected notes

## SETDYNAMIC
SETDYNAMIC VALUE/A,UPDATE/S

Change the dynamics setting.
- VALUE -- Numeric value 0-127 (MIDI velocity), or PPP, PP, P, MP, MF, F, FF, FFF
- UPDATE -- Also update any currently selected notes

## SETTUPLET
SETTUPLET VALUE/A,UPDATE/S

Change the tuplet setting in the tool window.
- VALUE -- By number: 0 (none), 3 (triplet), 5 (quintuplet), 7 (septuplet)
  Or by keyword: NONE, TRIPLET, QUINTUPLET, SEPTUPLET
- UPDATE -- Also update any currently selected notes

## REQUESTNOTIFY
REQUESTNOTIFY TITLE/K,PROMPT

Open a 1-button (OK) requester to display a message.
- TITLE -- Window title
- PROMPT -- Message text

Example: REQUESTNOTIFY TITLE "Info" "Score has 42 measures"

## REQUESTRESPONSE
REQUESTRESPONSE TITLE/K,PROMPT,DEFAULT/K/N,BUTTONS/K

Open a 2-button requester for yes/no questions. Returns 1 or 0 in RESULT.
- TITLE -- Window title
- PROMPT -- Question text
- DEFAULT -- Default button (1=left, 0=right)
- BUTTONS -- Button labels separated by |

Example: REQUESTRESPONSE TITLE "Confirm" "Transpose all?" BUTTONS "Yes|No"

## REQUESTNUM
REQUESTNUM TITLE/K,PROMPT,DEFAULT/K/N,BUTTONS/K

Prompt the user for a number. Returns the number in RESULT.
- TITLE -- Window title
- PROMPT -- Prompt text
- DEFAULT -- Default value
- BUTTONS -- Button labels

## REQUESTSTRING
REQUESTSTRING TITLE/K,PROMPT,DEFAULT/K,BUTTONS/K

Prompt the user for a string. Returns the string in RESULT.
- TITLE -- Window title
- PROMPT -- Prompt text
- DEFAULT -- Default string value
- BUTTONS -- Button labels

## REQUESTFILE
REQUESTFILE TITLE/K,PATH/K,FILE/K,PATTERN/K

Prompt the user for a filename. Returns the full path in RESULT.
- TITLE -- Requester title
- PATH -- Initial directory
- FILE -- Initial filename
- PATTERN -- AmigaDOS pattern filter (e.g. #?.CMUS)

Example: REQUESTFILE TITLE "Open Score" PATH "Work:Scores" PATTERN "#?.CMUS"

## GOTO
GOTO TRACK/K/N,STAFF/K/N,MEASURE/K/N,CHORD/K/N,CLOCK/K/N,HIDDEN/S

Move the cursor to a specified location.
- TRACK -- Track number (1-based)
- STAFF -- Staff number (1-based). Note: STAFF = TRACK / 2
- MEASURE -- Measure number (1-based)
- CHORD -- Chord position within measure
- CLOCK -- Clock tick position within measure
- HIDDEN -- Allow moving to hidden items

Example: GOTO MEASURE 5 STAFF 1
Example: GOTO TRACK 2 MEASURE 1

## POSITION
POSITION SOF/S,EOF/S,SOM/S,EOM/S,HIDDEN/S

Move cursor to a boundary position.
- SOF -- Start of file (first item in score)
- EOF -- End of file (last item in score)
- SOM -- Start of current measure
- EOM -- End of current measure
- HIDDEN -- Allow positioning at hidden items

Example: POSITION SOF

## NEXT
NEXT EVENT/S,NOTE/S,INTERVAL/S,CHORD/S,MEASURE/S,STAFF/S,TRACK/S,SELECTED/N,HIDDEN/S,COUNT/N

Move cursor to the next item.
- EVENT -- Next event of any type
- NOTE -- Next note
- INTERVAL -- Next interval/note within a chord
- CHORD -- Next chord position
- MEASURE -- Next measure
- STAFF -- Next staff
- TRACK -- Next track
- SELECTED -- Move to next selected (1) or unselected (0) item
- HIDDEN -- Include hidden items
- COUNT -- Number of steps to move

Example: NEXT NOTE
Example: NEXT MEASURE COUNT 4

## PREVIOUS
PREVIOUS EVENT/S,NOTE/S,INTERVAL/S,CHORD/S,MEASURE/S,STAFF/S,TRACK/S,SELECTED/N,HIDDEN/S,COUNT/N

Move cursor to the previous item. Same parameters as NEXT.

Example: PREVIOUS MEASURE

## SELECTITEM
SELECTITEM ADD/S,REMOVE/S,TOGGLE/S

Select the item after the cursor.
- ADD -- Add to current selection (don't deselect others)
- REMOVE -- Remove from selection
- TOGGLE -- Toggle selection state

## SELECTALL
SELECTALL

Select all items in the score.

## DESELECTALL
DESELECTALL

Deselect all selected items.

## INSERTITEM
INSERTITEM TYPE,TRACK/K/N,DURATION/K,CLOCKS/K/N,DOTS/K/N,TUPLET/K/N,ACCIDENTAL/K,OCTAVE/K/N,LINE/K/N,PITCH/K/N,LETTER/K,NOTESTEM/K,LOUDNESS/K/N,FONT/K,RATE/K/N,SELECTED/N,HIDDEN/S,NOFIX/S

Add an item to the score at the cursor position.

Item types:
  NOTE      New chord (default)
  REST      Rest
  INTERVAL  Add a note to an existing chord
  DYNAMIC   Dynamic value
  TEMPO     Tempo marking
  BAR       Bar line
  TEXT      Text annotation
  CLEF      Clef change
  KEY       Key signature change
  TIME      Time signature change
  REHEARSAL Rehearsal marking

Attributes for all items:
- TRACK -- Track number to create the item on
- SELECTED -- Non-zero to select, zero to deselect
- HIDDEN -- Create without updating display (faster for batch operations)
- NOFIX -- Disable re-sorting (use with RESORTEVENTS for batch operations)

Attributes for notes and rests:
- DURATION -- Format: [division][:tuplet][.dots]
  Divisions: D (double whole), W or 1 (whole), H or 2 (half),
  O or 4 (quarter), 8 (eighth), 16, 32, 64
  Tuplets: 0 (none), 1 (triplet), 2 (quintuplet), 3 (septuplet)
  Dots: 0, 1, or 2
  Example: "32:3.2" = 32nd note double-dotted triplet, "D:3" = double whole triplet
- CLOCKS -- Duration in clock ticks (alternative to DURATION)

Attributes for notes only:
- ACCIDENTAL -- NONE, FLAT, NATURAL, SHARP
- OCTAVE -- Octave number (0 = middle C octave)
- LINE -- Staff line (0=middle, positive=higher, negative=lower)
- PITCH -- MIDI pitch number (0-127)
- LETTER -- Note letter: A, B, C, D, E, F, G
- NOTESTEM -- Stem direction: UP, DOWN

Attributes for dynamics only:
- LOUDNESS -- MIDI velocity (0-127)
  PPP=0-10, PP=11-19, P=20-31, MP=32-47,
  MF=48-63, F=64-81, FF=82-107, FFF=108-127
- FONT -- Text font name (for TEXT type)
- RATE -- Tempo in BPM (for TEMPO type)

Example: INSERTITEM NOTE DURATION 2 LINE 3 NOTESTEM UP
Example: INSERTITEM NOTE LETTER C OCTAVE 4 DURATION QUARTER
Example: INSERTITEM INTERVAL LETTER E OCTAVE 4 (add to chord)
Example: INSERTITEM REST DURATION HALF
Example: INSERTITEM TEMPO RATE 120

## INSERTMEASURE
INSERTMEASURE

Add a new empty measure after the current measure.

## CLEAR
CLEAR FORCE/S

Delete all data from the score.
- FORCE -- Clear without confirmation

## ERASE
ERASE

Delete all currently selected items.

## CLEARMOD
CLEARMOD

Remove all accidentals and tuplets from selected items.

## DELBACKWD
DELBACKWD

Delete the item before the cursor.

## DELFWD
DELFWD

Delete the item after the cursor.

## DELETEMEASURE
DELETEMEASURE COUNT/N

Delete measure(s) starting from the current measure.
- COUNT -- Number of measures to delete (default: 1)

## CHANGEITEM
CHANGEITEM TYPE,TRACK/K/N,DURATION/K,CLOCKS/K/N,DOTS/K/N,TUPLET/K/N,ACCIDENTAL/K,OCTAVE/K/N,LINE/K/N,PITCH/K/N,LETTER/K,NOTESTEM/K,LOUDNESS/K/N,FONT/K,RATE/K/N,SELECTED/N,HIDDEN/S,NOFIX/S

Modify the item after the cursor. Only specified parameters are changed.
NOTE: CHANGEITEM is not undoable.

- NOFIX -- Disable re-sorting during batch edits (use with RESORTEVENTS)

Attributes for all items:
- SELECTED -- Non-zero to select, zero to deselect
- HIDDEN -- Change without updating display (much faster for batch edits)

Attributes for notes and rests:
- DURATION -- Format: [division][:tuplet][.dots]
  Valid divisions: D (double whole), W or 1 (whole), H or 2 (half),
  O or 4 (quarter), 8 (eighth), 16, 32, 64
  Valid tuplets: 0 (none), 1 (triplet), 2 (quintuplet), 3 (septuplet)
  Valid dots: 0, 1, or 2

Attributes for notes only:
- ACCIDENTAL -- NONE, FLAT, NATURAL, SHARP
- OCTAVE -- Octave number (0 = middle C octave)
- LINE -- Staff line number (0=middle line, positive=higher, negative=lower)
- PITCH -- MIDI pitch number (0-127)
- LETTER -- Note letter: A, B, C, D, E, F, G
- NOTESTEM -- Stem direction: UP, DOWN, TOGGLE

Attributes for dynamics only:
- LOUDNESS -- MIDI volume (0-127)

Example: CHANGEITEM DURATION HALF
Example: CHANGEITEM LETTER D OCTAVE 5
Example: CHANGEITEM OCTAVE (-1)

## CHANGESELECTED
CHANGESELECTED TYPE,TRACK/K/N,DURATION/K,CLOCKS/K/N,DOTS/K/N,TUPLET/K/N,ACCIDENTAL/K,OCTAVE/K/N,LINE/K/N,PITCH/K/N,LETTER/K,NOTESTEM/K,LOUDNESS/K/N,FONT/K,RATE/K/N,SELECTED/N,HIDDEN/S,NOFIX/S

Modify all currently selected items. Same parameters as CHANGEITEM.

Example: CHANGESELECTED LOUDNESS 100
Example: CHANGESELECTED NOTESTEM DOWN

## CHANGETONE
CHANGETONE HALFSTEP/K/N,LEVEL/K/N,OCTAVE/K/N

Change the pitch of selected notes.
- HALFSTEP -- Transpose by N half steps (positive=up, negative=down)
- LEVEL -- Transpose by N staff levels (diatonic steps)
- OCTAVE -- Transpose by N octaves

Example: CHANGETONE HALFSTEP 7 (transpose up a fifth)
Example: CHANGETONE OCTAVE -1 (transpose down one octave)

## FLIPNOTESTEM
FLIPNOTESTEM DIRECTION

Flip the direction of selected note stems.
- DIRECTION -- UP, DOWN, or TOGGLE

Example: FLIPNOTESTEM TOGGLE

## GROUPITEM
GROUPITEM ACTION/A,TYPE/A,DIRECTION

Add or remove grouping. The group to add or delete must be selected first.
- ACTION -- ADD or DELETE
- TYPE -- TIE, BEAM, SLUR, OCTAVE, CRESCENDO, DECRESCENDO
- DIRECTION -- UP or DOWN (default: UP)

Example: GROUPITEM ADD TIE
Example: GROUPITEM ADD BEAM UP
Example: GROUPITEM DELETE SLUR

## DOUBLETIME
DOUBLETIME

Double the duration of all selected notes (e.g. quarter -> half).

## HALFTIME
HALFTIME

Halve the duration of all selected notes (e.g. quarter -> eighth).

## INVERTCHORD
INVERTCHORD DIRECTION

Invert a selected chord up or down.
- DIRECTION -- UP or DOWN

Example: INVERTCHORD UP
Example: INVERTCHORD DOWN

## JOINMEASURE
JOINMEASURE

Join the current measure with the next measure into one.

## SPLITMEASURE
SPLITMEASURE

Split the current measure into two at the cursor position.

## REALIGNMEASURE
REALIGNMEASURE

Realign note spacing in the current measure.

## SETBARATTR
SETBARATTR BEGINSECTION/S,ENDSECTION/S,ENDING1/K,ENDING2/K,BEGINREPEAT/K,ENDREPEAT/K,DOUBLEBAR/K

Change bar line attributes for all measures in the current selection range.
- BEGINSECTION -- Sets the first bar in the selection as section beginning
- ENDSECTION -- Sets the last bar in the selection as section ending
- ENDING1 -- First ending bracket: ON, OFF, or TOGGLE
- ENDING2 -- Second ending bracket: ON, OFF, or TOGGLE
- BEGINREPEAT -- Begin repeat: ON, OFF, or TOGGLE
- ENDREPEAT -- End repeat: ON, OFF, or TOGGLE
- DOUBLEBAR -- Double bar line: ON, OFF, or TOGGLE

Example: SETBARATTR BEGINREPEAT ON
Example: SETBARATTR ENDING1 ON

## SETCLEF
SETCLEF TYPE/A,STAFF/N/A,START/N,END/N

Change the clef for a staff at a particular measure.
- TYPE -- NONE, TREBLE, BASS, ALTO, TENOR
  NONE removes the clef change; the effective clef is derived from previous measures.
- STAFF -- Staff number (1-based)
- START -- Starting measure number (default: 0)
- END -- Ending measure. If omitted, effect continues until the next clef change.

Example: SETCLEF TREBLE 1 1 999
Example: SETCLEF BASS 1 3

## SETKEYSIGNATURE
SETKEYSIGNATURE TYPE/A,STAFF/N/A,START/N,END/N,TRANSPOSE/K

Change the key signature of a particular staff at a particular measure.
- TYPE -- Key name (use hyphens in compound names):
  Major: C-MAJOR, G-MAJOR, D-MAJOR, A-MAJOR, E-MAJOR, B-MAJOR,
         F-SHARP-MAJOR, C-SHARP-MAJOR, F-MAJOR, B-FLAT-MAJOR,
         E-FLAT-MAJOR, A-FLAT-MAJOR, D-FLAT-MAJOR, G-FLAT-MAJOR,
         C-FLAT-MAJOR
  Minor: A-MINOR, E-MINOR, B-MINOR, F-SHARP-MINOR, C-SHARP-MINOR,
         G-SHARP-MINOR, D-SHARP-MINOR, A-SHARP-MINOR, D-MINOR,
         G-MINOR, C-MINOR, F-MINOR, B-FLAT-MINOR, E-FLAT-MINOR,
         A-FLAT-MINOR
  NONE -- Removes key signature; effective key derived from previous measures.
- STAFF -- Staff number (1-based)
- START -- Starting measure (default: 0)
- END -- Ending measure. If omitted, effect continues until the next key change.
- TRANSPOSE -- YES or NO. Transpose existing notes to match new key

Example: SETKEYSIGNATURE C-FLAT-MAJOR 0 0
Example: SETKEYSIGNATURE G-MAJOR 1 1 999
Example: SETKEYSIGNATURE B-FLAT-MAJOR 1 5 999 TRANSPOSE YES

## SETTIMESIGNATURE
SETTIMESIGNATURE BEATS/N/A,DURATION/N/A,MEASURE/N

Change the time signature.
- BEATS -- Number of beats per measure (the "top" number).
  If 0, deletes the time signature change; the effective time signature
  is derived from previous measures.
- DURATION -- Beat duration (the "bottom" number): 4=quarter, 8=eighth, 2=half, etc.
- MEASURE -- Starting measure number. All measures from that point until the
  next time signature change will be affected.

Example: SETTIMESIGNATURE 3 4 (3/4 time)
Example: SETTIMESIGNATURE 6 8 1 (6/8 from measure 1)
Example: SETTIMESIGNATURE 4 4 8 1 (4/4 starting at measure 8)

## SETSTAFF
SETSTAFF STAFF/N/A,ATTR/A,VALUE/A

Change staff attributes.
- STAFF -- Staff number (1-based)
- ATTR -- Attribute name:
  SOUND            "Staff Sound On" checkmark (TRUE/FALSE)
  HIDDEN           "Staff Hidden" checkmark (TRUE/FALSE)
  HIDEINSTRUMENTS  "Hide Instruments" checkmark (TRUE/FALSE)
  HIDESIGNATURES   "Hide Time Signatures" checkmark (TRUE/FALSE)
  SHOWSTYLES       "Show Play Styles" checkmark (TRUE/FALSE)
  SPLIT            Split measure lines (TRUE/FALSE)
  TOPBRACKET       Staff has a bracket top (TRUE/FALSE)
  BOTTOMBRACKET    Staff has a bracket bottom (TRUE/FALSE)
  BRACE            Staff has bracket top and bottom (TRUE/FALSE)
  TRANSPOSITION    Staff transposition (numeric value)
  STAFFHEIGHT      Total height of staff (numeric value)
  STAFFVOFFSET     Space above staff (numeric value)
- VALUE -- TRUE/FALSE for checkmark attributes, numeric for others

Example: SETSTAFF 1 HIDEINSTRUMENTS TRUE
Example: SETSTAFF 1 TRANSPOSITION 9
Example: SETSTAFF 1 HIDDEN TRUE

## GETATTR
GETATTR OBJECT/A,NAME,FIELD

Get information about DeluxeMusic's status. Returns value in RESULT.
- OBJECT -- Object type to query (see below)
- NAME -- Specific object name (if omitted, queries the current object)
- FIELD -- Specific field (if omitted, returns all fields for that object)

Objects and their fields:

APPLICATION:
  VERSION        Version number of the program
  SCREEN         Name of the screen

PROJECTS:
  COUNT          Total number of open projects
  [number]       Name of a specific project by index

PROJECT:
  AREXX          ARexx port name for this document
  FILENAME       Complete filename with path
  FILE           File name only (without path)
  PATH           Drawer path only (without filename)
  FILEPATTERN    Current pattern in file requester
  CHANGES        Document has been modified (TRUE/FALSE)
  FEEDBACKTYPE   Feedback type (0 to 2)
  FLASHNOTES     "Flash notes" checkmark state
  TURNPAGES      "Turn pages" checkmark state
  PLAYERPIANO    "Player piano" checkmark state
  REPEATPLAY     "Repeat play" checkmark state
  CHROMATICDRAG  "Chromatic drag" checkmark state

WINDOWS:
  COUNT          Total number of open windows
  [number]       Name of a specific window by index

WINDOW:
  LEFT           Left edge coordinate
  TOP            Top edge coordinate
  WIDTH          Width in pixels
  HEIGHT         Height in pixels
  TITLE          Window title
  MIN.WIDTH      Minimum width
  MAX.WIDTH      Maximum width
  MIN.HEIGHT     Minimum height
  MAX.HEIGHT     Maximum height
  SCREEN         Screen name of the window

SCREEN:
  LEFT           Left edge of screen
  TOP            Top edge of screen
  WIDTH          Width of screen
  HEIGHT         Height of screen
  DEPTH          Depth (number of bitplanes)
  TITLE          Title of screen

SCORE:
  MEASURES       Number of measures in the score
  LASTUSEDBAR    Last used bar in the score
  BARSPERLINE    Bars per line setting
  STAVES         Number of staves in the score

Example: GETATTR APPLICATION "" VERSION
Example: GETATTR PROJECT "" FILENAME
Example: GETATTR SCORE "" MEASURES
Example: GETATTR SCORE "CLEOPHA" MEASURES
Example: GETATTR WINDOW "" LEFT

## GETERRORINFO
GETERRORINFO ERROR/N/A

Get a text description of an error number. Returns description in RESULT.
- ERROR -- Error number to look up

## GETPOSITION
GETPOSITION FIELD

Get current cursor position. Returns value in RESULT.
If FIELD is omitted, all position parameters are returned.

- FIELD -- Which attribute to query:
  MEASURE   Current measure number
  STAFF     Current staff number
  TRACK     Current track number
  CHORD     Current chord within the measure
  INTERVAL  Interval number in the chord
  TIME      Clock time of event, relative to measure start

Example: GETPOSITION MEASURE
Example: GETPOSITION TRACK

## GETITEMATTR
GETITEMATTR FIELD

Get information about the item just after the cursor. Returns value in RESULT.
If FIELD is omitted, all parameters are returned.

All items:
  ITEM.TYPE       Current item type
  ITEM.TRACK      Track number of the current item
  ITEM.START      Start time of item in ticks
  ITEM.XPOS       X position of item on screen
  ITEM.SELECTED   Item selection state

Note items (Note track only):
  NOTE.DIVISION     Division (D=double whole, 1=whole, 2=half, 4=quarter, 8, 16, 32, 64)
  NOTE.TUPLET       Tuplet value
  NOTE.DOTS         Number of dots
  NOTE.ACCIDENTAL   Accidental type
  NOTE.LEVEL        Staff line level
  NOTE.PITCH        MIDI note pitch (0-127)
  NOTE.STYLE        Note style
  NOTE.INSTRUMENT   Note instrument number
  NOTE.BEAMHEIGHT   Note beam height
  NOTE.FIXEDPOS     TRUE if note position was manually specified
  NOTE.BEAMOUT      TRUE if beamed to next note
  NOTE.TIEOUT       TRUE if tied to next note
  NOTE.TIEDOWN      TRUE if tie curves downward
  NOTE.STEMDOWN     TRUE if stem points downward

Instrument items (Instrument track only):
  INSTRUMENT.NUMBER   Instrument number in table

Tempo items (Tempo track only):
  TEMPO.VALUE         New tempo value (BPM)

Dynamic items:
  DYNAMIC.VOLUME      MIDI volume (0-127)
  DYNAMIC.VPOS        Vertical position of event

Group items:
  GROUP.ENDVOL        End volume for crescendos (0-127)
  GROUP.GROUPDOWN     TRUE if group direction is down

Example: GETITEMATTR ITEM.TYPE
Example: GETITEMATTR NOTE.PITCH
Example: GETITEMATTR TEMPO.VALUE

## GETCLEF
GETCLEF STAFF/N/A,MEASURE/N,EFFECTIVE/S

Get clef information. Returns clef type in RESULT.
- STAFF -- Staff number (1-based)
- MEASURE -- Measure number (default: current)
- EFFECTIVE -- Return the clef in effect at that point (may be set in an earlier measure)

## GETKEYSIGNATURE
GETKEYSIGNATURE STAFF/N/A,MEASURE/N,EFFECTIVE/S

Get key signature. Returns key name in RESULT.
- STAFF -- Staff number
- MEASURE -- Measure number
- EFFECTIVE -- Return the key in effect at that point

## GETSTAFF
GETSTAFF STAFF/N/A,ATTR/A

Get staff attribute value. Returns value in RESULT.
- STAFF -- Staff number (1-based)
- ATTR -- Attribute name:
  SOUND            "Staff sound on" checkmark
  HIDDEN           "Staff Hidden" checkmark
  HIDEINSTRUMENTS  "Hide Instruments" checkmark
  HIDESIGNATURES   "Hide Time Signatures" checkmark
  SHOWSTYLES       "Show Play Styles" checkmark
  SPLIT            Split measure lines
  TOPBRACKET       Staff has a bracket top
  BOTTOMBRACKET    Staff has a bracket bottom
  BRACE            Staff has a brace (bracket top and bottom)
  TRANSPOSITION    Staff transposition value
  STAFFHEIGHT      Total height (space above + space below)
  STAFFVOFFSET     Space above staff
  NAME, CHANNEL, INSTRUMENT, TRANSPOSE, VOLUME, PAN, VISIBLE

Example: GETSTAFF 1 NAME
Example: GETSTAFF 1 STAFFHEIGHT
Example: GETSTAFF 2 TRANSPOSITION

## GETTIMESIGNATURE
GETTIMESIGNATURE MEASURE/N,EFFECTIVE/S

Get time signature. Returns "beats/duration" in RESULT (e.g. "4/4").
- MEASURE -- Measure number
- EFFECTIVE -- Return the time signature in effect at that point

## RESORTEVENTS
RESORTEVENTS

Re-sort all events after batch editing with NOFIX.
Recommended batch editing pattern:
1. LOCKGUI
2. LOCKDISPLAY
3. Edit items with NOFIX flag
4. RESORTEVENTS
5. UNLOCKDISPLAY
6. UNLOCKGUI

## RX
RX CONSOLE/S,ASYNC/S,COMMAND/F

Execute an ARexx script file.
- CONSOLE -- Open a console window for the script
- ASYNC -- Run asynchronously (don't wait for completion)
- COMMAND -- Script filename and arguments (rest of line)

Example: RX "Rexx:Transpose.rexx"

## RXS
RXS CONSOLE/S,ASYNC/S,COMMAND/F

Execute an ARexx command string directly.
- CONSOLE -- Open a console window
- ASYNC -- Run asynchronously
- COMMAND -- ARexx code to execute (rest of line)

Example: RXS "say 'Hello from DMusic'"

## ABORTSCRIPTS
ABORTSCRIPTS

Abort all currently executing ARexx scripts.

## CMDSHELL
CMDSHELL

Open the interactive ARexx command shell window.

## HELP
HELP COMMAND

Display usage information for an ARexx command. Returns help text in RESULT.
- COMMAND -- Command name to get help for (omit for list of all commands)

Example: HELP INSERTITEM

## LEARN
LEARN FILE/K,STOP/S

Start or stop recording a macro.
- FILE -- Save macro to this file
- STOP -- Stop recording

Example: LEARN FILE "Rexx:MyMacro.rexx" (start recording)
Example: LEARN STOP (stop recording)

## PLAYMACRO
PLAYMACRO

Execute the last recorded macro.

## SAVEMACRO
SAVEMACRO FILE/K

Save the last recorded macro to a file.
- FILE -- Destination filename

Example: SAVEMACRO FILE "Rexx:MyMacro.rexx"
